# Trivy ignore file — curated, justified CVE risk acceptances.
# Each entry MUST have a rationale. Review on every dependency bump.
# Auto-discovered by Trivy when scanning with this directory as the
# working dir (or via TRIVY_IGNOREFILE).
#
# Currently EMPTY for Python packages: the langchain 1.x migration
# cleared every previously-residual langchain-stack CVE. `pip-audit`
# and `trivy` both report zero Python vulnerabilities.
#
# OS-package CVEs in the Debian base have no upstream fix available
# (`FixedVersion` empty) and are not listed here — they are mitigated by
# the container hardening (non-root, read-only fs, dropped caps, minimal
# package set) and tracked in docs/security.md. Add an entry here only
# with a written, reviewed rationale.
